  "<section class=\"course-page\" id=\"lesson-07\" data-chapter11-complete=\"drugs\" hidden=\"\">\n<div class=\"p2-topic\">\n<header class=\"page-header\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-474\">Learn \u00b7 Chapter 11</p>\n<h1 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-475\">Drugs at the synapse</h1>\n<p class=\"lesson-question\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-476\">How can a drug change communication at a synapse?</p>\n<div class=\"goal-strip\"><div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-01\">Learning goal</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-02\">I can predict how changing one step at a synapse affects the signal.</p></div>\n<div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-03\">Before you begin</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-04\">Review neurotransmitter release, receptor binding and removal in Lesson 6.</p></div></div>\n<details class=\"page-guide\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-guide-summary\"><strong>How to complete this lesson</strong> \u2014 Learn \u2192 practise \u2192 required check \u2192 finish</summary>\n<div>\n<ol>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-guide-01\"><strong>Start with the lesson.</strong> Read the learning goal and \u201cBefore you begin,\u201d then work through the explanation, diagrams and examples below. The embedded textbook is optional support: open it when you want another explanation or a closer look at a figure.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-guide-02\"><strong>Use the learning goal and starting reminder.</strong> The learning goal above tells you what you must be able to explain. Read \u201cBefore you begin\u201d next to connect this lesson to what you already know.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-guide-03\"><strong>Work through the online lesson in order.</strong> Read each teaching section and study its diagrams, examples and comparisons. Select an underlined biology term when you need its meaning. Use the video or Vocabulary help when an idea is still unclear.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-guide-04\"><strong>Complete the required chapter check.</strong> Open the check near the bottom and select Start. For multiple choice, select Check answer; a correct answer unlocks the related writing. Answer in your own words and select Save written response for every response box.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-guide-05\"><strong>Submit only when the required work is complete.</strong> Check that every required item has been attempted and every written response is saved. Then select Submit and finish. This stops the timer, records the completed run in All My Work and updates chapter progress.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-guide-06\"><strong>Use optional practice only when it helps.</strong> Optional source practice and Practice &amp; Review activities can help you study, but they do not count toward the 12 required chapter checks.</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-guide-07\"><strong>Expected work:</strong> complete the lesson and submit the required chapter check. Use optional reading, videos and practice when they help. Drafts save automatically as you work in this browser.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n<div class=\"textbook-band\"><div><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-05\">Optional embedded reading</p><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-06\"><strong>Chapter 11 \u00b7 p. 384</strong></p></div><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"25\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-07\">Open at p. 384</a></div>\n<p class=\"lesson-term-strip\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-teacher-voice-terms\"><strong>Key terms:</strong> neurotransmitter \u00b7 receptor \u00b7 reuptake \u00b7 cholinesterase</p>\n<details class=\"lesson-vocabulary-help\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-teacher-voice-vocab-summary\">Vocabulary help</summary>\n<section class=\"lesson-words\" aria-labelledby=\"lesson-07-anchor-words\"><p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-08\">Key terms</p><h2 id=\"lesson-07-anchor-words\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-09\">Words for this lesson</h2><p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-10\">Use these definitions when you need help with a term.</p><dl>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"agonist\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-07\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-11\">agonist</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-12\">a substance that activates a receptor</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"antagonist\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-07\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-13\">antagonist</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-14\">a substance that blocks receptor activation</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"reuptake\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-07\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-15\">reuptake</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-16\">taking a released neurotransmitter back into a cell</dd></div>\n<div><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"cholinesterase\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-07\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-17\">cholinesterase</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-18\">an enzyme that breaks down acetylcholine</dd></div>\n</dl></section>\n<details class=\"lesson-term-inventory\"><summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-19\">More vocabulary for this lesson</summary><div><section aria-labelledby=\"lesson-07-all-terms\"><h3 id=\"lesson-07-all-terms\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-20\">Lesson vocabulary</h3><dl><div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-21\">synapse \u00b7 neurotransmitter \u00b7 receptor \u00b7 agonist \u00b7 antagonist \u00b7 reuptake \u00b7 acetylcholine \u00b7 cholinesterase \u00b7 mechanism</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-setup-22\">Select an underlined term for its definition. Your vocabulary writing is saved in Process Collection.</dd></div></dl></section></div></details>\n</details>\n</header>\n",
  "\n\n<details class=\"activity-disclosure\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-check-toggle\">Open chapter check: Drugs at the synapse</summary>\n<section class=\"activity\" data-activity=\"check-drugs\" data-activity-mode=\"paired\" data-required-check=\"\">\n<h2 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-494\">Check: Drugs at the synapse</h2>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-495\">Chapter check \u00b7 Select Start when ready. The elapsed timer includes breaks; Submit and finish stops it. Redo preserves earlier attempts.</p>\n<div class=\"save-row\">\n<button type=\"button\" data-start=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-496\">Start</button>\n<output data-timer=\"\">Not started</output>\n</div>\n<fieldset data-run-body=\"\" disabled=\"\">\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"check-drugs-mc\">\n<h3 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-497\">The transmission of the nerve impulse across a synapse is accomplished by the release of a neurotransmitter</h3>\n<label class=\"choice\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-498\">\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"check-drugs-mc\" value=\"QUES_51667_82706_A275458\" data-answer=\"\"> from the cell body of the pre-synaptic neuron to the Schwann cell of the post synaptic neuron.</label>\n<label class=\"choice\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-499\">\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"check-drugs-mc\" value=\"QUES_51667_82706_A275459\" data-answer=\"\"> from the Schwann cell of the pre-synaptic neuron to the cell body of the post synaptic neuron.</label>\n<label class=\"choice\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-500\">\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"check-drugs-mc\" value=\"QUES_51667_82706_A275460\" data-answer=\"\"> from the dendrite of the pre-synaptic neuron to the axon of the post synaptic neuron.</label>\n<label class=\"choice\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-501\">\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"check-drugs-mc\" value=\"QUES_51667_82706_A275461\" data-answer=\"\"> from the axon of the pre-synaptic neuron to the dendrite of the post synaptic neuron.</label>\n<button type=\"button\" data-check=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-502\">Check answer</button>\n<p data-feedback=\"\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-503\">\n</p>\n<fieldset class=\"paired-writing\" data-unlock=\"check-drugs-mc\" disabled=\"\">\n<legend>Explain the related idea</legend>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-504\">\nHypothesize how overproduction of cholinesterase might affect the body. Explain your answer.</p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-505\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"25\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-506\">Textbook p. 384</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"check-drugs-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-507\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"check-drugs-written\" data-writing=\"check-drugs-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"check-drugs-written-limit check-drugs-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"check-drugs-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-508\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-509\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"check-drugs-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-510\">\n</p>\n</fieldset>\n</div>\n</fieldset>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-run=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-511\">Submit and finish</button> <button type=\"button\" data-redo=\"\" hidden=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-512\">Redo activity</button>\n<p data-run-status=\"\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-513\">\n</p>\n</section>\n</details>\n<div class=\"content-section\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-516\">Thought Lab 11.1 \u2014 The Effect of Drugs on Neurons and Synapses \u2014 <a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"12\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-517\">Textbook p. 371</a>\n</p>\n</div>\n<details class=\"activity-disclosure\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l07-practice-toggle\">Open optional source practice: Drugs at the synapse</summary>\n<section class=\"activity\" data-activity=\"practice-drugs\" data-activity-mode=\"writing\">\n<h2 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-518\">Source practice: Drugs at the synapse</h2>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-519\">Optional source practice \u00b7 Select Start when ready. The elapsed timer includes breaks; Submit and finish stops it. Redo preserves earlier attempts.</p>\n<div class=\"save-row\">\n<button type=\"button\" data-start=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-520\">Start</button>\n<output data-timer=\"\">Not started</output>\n</div>\n<fieldset data-run-body=\"\" disabled=\"\">\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-review111-q1\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-521\">\nCopy the letters A through H into your notebook. Identify the division of the nervous system that is represented by each letter.</p>\n<figure class=\"learning-figure question-figure\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-522\">\n<a class=\"figure-open\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"assets/source/chapter11-drugs-1.png\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-523\">\n<img alt=\"Original diagram for Section 11.1 Review, question 1. Keep these original labels when answering.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/source/chapter11-drugs-1.png\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-524\">\n</a>\n<figcaption>diagram for Section 11.1 Review, question 1. Keep these original labels when answering.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-525\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"25\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-526\">Textbook p. 384</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-review111-q1-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-527\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-review111-q1-written\" data-writing=\"source-review111-q1-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-review111-q1-written-limit source-review111-q1-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-review111-q1-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-528\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-529\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-review111-q1-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-530\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-review111-q2\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-531\">\nAnalyze the following statement: \u201cThe neuron conducts impulses in the same way as electricity moves through a wire.\u201d Is a nerve impulse like electricity? Prepare a table that compares a nerve impulse to the movement of an electric current along a wire.</p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-532\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"25\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-533\">Textbook p. 384</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-review111-q2-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-534\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-review111-q2-written\" data-writing=\"source-review111-q2-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-review111-q2-written-limit source-review111-q2-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-review111-q2-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-535\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-536\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-review111-q2-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-537\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-review111-q3\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-538\">\nCompare the structure and functions of myelinated neurons and unmyelinated neurons.</p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-539\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"25\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-540\">Textbook p. 384</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-review111-q3-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-541\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-review111-q3-written\" data-writing=\"source-review111-q3-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-review111-q3-written-limit source-review111-q3-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-review111-q3-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-542\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-543\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-review111-q3-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-544\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-review111-q4\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-545\">\nUsing a diagram, explain how a neuron establishes the resting membrane potential. What is the value of this in mV?</p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-546\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"25\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-547\">Textbook p. 384</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-review111-q4-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-548\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-review111-q4-written\" data-writing=\"source-review111-q4-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-review111-q4-written-limit source-review111-q4-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-review111-q4-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-549\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-550\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-review111-q4-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-551\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-review111-q5\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-552\">\nExamine the graph below, and answer the questions that follow.</p>\n<figure class=\"learning-figure question-figure\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-553\">\n<a class=\"figure-open\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"assets/source/chapter11-drugs-2.png\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-554\">\n<img alt=\"Original diagram for Section 11.1 Review, question 5. Keep these original labels when answering.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/source/chapter11-drugs-2.png\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-555\">\n</a>\n<figcaption>diagram for Section 11.1 Review, question 5. Keep these original labels when answering.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<ol class=\"subquestions\" type=\"a\">\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-556\">In your notebook, indicate the specific events that are occurring at 1, 2, 3, and 4.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-557\">At which area of the graph are sodium ions rapidly entering the neuron?</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-558\">At which area of the graph are potassium ions rapidly leaving the neuron?</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-559\">At which area of the graph is the sodium ion concentration higher outside than inside the neuron?</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-560\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"25\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-561\">Textbook p. 384</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-review111-q5-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-562\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-review111-q5-written\" data-writing=\"source-review111-q5-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-review111-q5-written-limit source-review111-q5-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-review111-q5-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-563\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-564\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-review111-q5-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-565\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-review111-q7\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-566\">\nUse word processing or spreadsheet software to construct a table to compare an excitatory response with an inhibitory response. Give an example of where these responses are complementary in the body. ICT</p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-567\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"25\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-568\">Textbook p. 384</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-review111-q7-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-569\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-review111-q7-written\" data-writing=\"source-review111-q7-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-review111-q7-written-limit source-review111-q7-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-review111-q7-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-570\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-571\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-review111-q7-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-572\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"question\" data-question=\"source-review111-q8\">\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-573\">\nCocaine affects a synapse by blocking the re-uptake of the neurotransmitter dopamine by the presynaptic neurons. Therefore, the levels of dopamine continue to build in the synapse, causing certain effects on the body.</p>\n<ol class=\"subquestions\" type=\"a\">\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-574\">Use word processing software to make a flowchart summarizing the usual events in the transmission of an impulse between the presynaptic and postsynaptic neurons. ICT</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-575\">Explain how cocaine interferes with neural transmission across the synapse.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-576\">Describe the natural role of dopamine in the brain.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-577\">Formulate a hypothesis about how cocaine could be addictive after only one use.\n<aside class=\"learning-note insight\">\n<strong data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-493\">For question 8(d):</strong> propose a possible explanation. A hypothesis is not proof that the outcome must occur after one exposure.</aside></li>\n\n</ol>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-578\">\n<a href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"25\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-579\">Textbook p. 384</a>\n</p>\n<label for=\"source-review111-q8-written\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-580\">Written response</label>\n<textarea id=\"source-review111-q8-written\" data-writing=\"source-review111-q8-written\" data-answer-limit=\"3200\" rows=\"6\" aria-describedby=\"source-review111-q8-written-limit source-review111-q8-written-status\"></textarea>\n<p id=\"source-review111-q8-written-limit\" class=\"muted\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-581\">Up to 3200 characters. Drafts can be longer, but must fit before submission. Writing is not automatically graded.</p>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-writing=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-582\">Save written response</button>\n<p data-writing-status=\"\" id=\"source-review111-q8-written-status\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-583\">\n</p>\n</div>\n</fieldset>\n<button type=\"button\" data-submit-run=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-584\">Submit and finish</button> <button type=\"button\" data-redo=\"\" hidden=\"\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-585\">Redo activity</button>\n<p data-run-status=\"\" role=\"status\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-586\">\n</p>\n</section>\n</details>\n<div class=\"content-section\">\n<a href=\"#lesson-06\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-587\">Previous: Synapses &amp; summation</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\"> \u00b7 </span><a href=\"#lesson-08\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-588\">Next: Peripheral control</a>\n<p class=\"textbook-practice-lesson-link\"><a href=\"#textbook-practice\" data-textbook-topic=\"lesson-07\">Optional textbook practice for Drugs at the synapse</a></p></div>\n</div>\n</section>"
